ghostlock-somalia
=================

This is an independent, device-specific research port and field-notes
repository for GhostLock (CVE-2026-43499).

Upstream exploit and technique:
  NebuSec (Nebula Security), "IonStack Part II — GhostLock"
  https://nebusec.ai/research/ionstack-part-2/
  https://github.com/NebuSec/CyberMeowfia
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Pixel/aarch64 adaptation:
  JingMatrix/pixel-ksu-root, commit 65762e7, Apache-2.0.
  https://github.com/JingMatrix/pixel-ksu-root
  The vendored upstream NOTICE is preserved where applicable.

OnePlus port / device matrix:
  JoinChang/ghostlock-oneplus, commit 9b2a7ba.
  https://github.com/JoinChang/ghostlock-oneplus

KernelSnitch heap-pointer side channel:
  Lukas Maar et al., TU Graz, NDSS 2025.
  https://github.com/isec-tugraz/KernelSnitch

This repository adds a Redmi A7 Pro 5G (somalia, Unisoc T8300) port,
per-boot P0 derivation, QEMU validation, and incident analyses. It does not
claim discovery of CVE-2026-43499.

No vendor firmware, vendor blobs, proprietary dexdumps, private keys, device
identifiers, or owner data are included.
